  nonce: 68cd  # 68cd
  message: "DONE 2026-09-13, PR #949, dev eb520bc07c.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, production path. The tests call compute_boundary_coverage\nitself and assert on the reason it returns, rather than grepping the source:\n\n  both blockers present (a bash launch plus an uncatalogued python module)\n    BEFORE: \"the analysis launches an external program at 1 call site(s) (id)\n             and cannot see what the launched program does, so whether this\n             I/O happens there was never examined\"\n    AFTER:  the same sentence, then \"; and it makes calls into 1 module(s)\n             that the I/O catalog could not classify (requests), which is what\n             withholds the qualified verdict the launches alone would have\n             earned\"\n\n  launch alone (the control): sentence UNCHANGED, no module blamed.\n\nTHE ORDERING RATIONALE IS PRESERVED, not traded away. The launch is still named\nfirst, and a test pins that: an uncatalogued module is a gap the reader can\nclose, an opaque launch is categorical, so naming the fixable one first would\nsend a reader on an errand that cannot succeed. This adds the second half of\nthe sentence.\n\nTHE CONTROL IS A REAL CONTROL. test_a_launch_alone_still_blames_no_module fails\non the lazy fix - appending the clause unconditionally - which would blame an\nempty module set on every launching repo.\n\n3083 passed, 1 skipped, 1 xfailed; 100% coverage on changed files.\n\nWHAT THIS WAS WORTH, concretely: the cron failure that surfaced WI-jabus named\ntwo subprocess launches and nothing else, and the thirteen names that actually\nwithheld the verdicts had to be recovered by monkeypatching\n_adjudicate_external_modules. The next such failure is diagnosable from its own\nlog.\n\nNOT DONE, left on the item as filed: exposing the unknown set as its own field\nin the JSON envelope, so a consumer reads it without parsing prose. That is a\nschema change (VERIFY_CLAIMS_SCHEMA_VERSION) and is a separate piece of work.\nRe-open or re-file if that half is wanted."  # 68cd
